## 5. The open Red finding: the sheet fixture does not fit the 264 px sheet limit

The Red pin of round 2 and the spec "The horizontal crop" rule 2 ask for opposite results for the
cast sheet fixture.

- The spec rule 2: the widest mask run of the head band, scaled, must be at most
  `cellWidth - 16` px. The sheet cell is 280 px wide, so the sheet limit is 264 px.
- The sheet fixture of `tests/sprout-cast-panel.test.ts` draws every lit front render as one
  rectangle from x 80 to x 176. The head band of that rectangle is 97 source px wide, and the
  sheet scale of the adult fixture is 3.5, so the head of Dad is 339.5 px wide. The head of the
  sheet fixture does not fit the 264 px limit, so the sheet refuses the fixture.
- The six failing cases are `sheet is 1544 x 900 with five figures at one scale and one baseline`,
  `F3 sheet refuses a head wider than its 280 px cell`, `F3 sheet caption includes the fifth cell
  crop state inside the sheet width`, `F3 sheet prints and captions cropped state for every cell`,
  `--sheet writes the sheet and no panel`, and `--all writes five panels and the sheet`. The
  second case expects the refusal to name `sprout-tom-kim`, and the script names
  `sprout-dad-kim` first, because the head of Dad is already too wide.
- The new case `F3 sheet uses the 264 px head-fit limit` passes. Its fixture draws a head of 100
  source px, which is 350 px at the sheet scale, and the sheet refuses it by name.
- The only threshold that accepts the sheet fixture and refuses the 350 px head is a limit between
  339.5 px and 350 px. No rule of the spec states such a limit, so the implementation keeps the
  264 px limit of the spec and of the adversarial finding.
- A probe with the same fixtures and a head of 37 source px, which is 129.5 px wide, shows that
  the sheet then writes: the caption ends at column 584 of 1544, the caption bytes change when the
  crop state of Lily changes, the sheet refuses the wide head of Tom by name, and the sheet
  refuses the 350 px head of Dad by name.
- The repair belongs to Red, because Red owns the test files. The repair is one line: the sheet
  fixture draws the lit front renders with a head of at most 75 source px, which is 264 px at the
  sheet scale. The panel cell is 440 px wide, so the panel cases of the same fixture stay valid.
- The PM may instead amend the spec, so that the sheet limit accepts a head of 339.5 px and
  refuses a head of 350 px. Green does not choose that limit without the amendment.

The two findings of the round 1 stay open as well, for the reason recorded in the T2 notes: F4,
where the Red pin and the adversarial finding ask for opposite results, and F12, where the plan
reason of the nearest-neighbour sampling was wrong.

